// SBFL-oriented coverage configuration.
//
// Coverage instrumentation is enabled by the command line. Suppress every non-core
// source family loaded by the simple-system target, leaving the CPU RTL listed
// below as the effective whitelist. Module inputs are disabled at their
// declaration lines: their toggles are stimulus/boundary coverage and cannot
// be attributed to a statement in that module. This also removes all clk/reset
// input toggle points.
//
// The line numbers below intentionally follow the current RTL revision. Update
// them when a module port list or one of the explicitly excluded blocks moves.

`verilator_config

coverage_off -file "*"

coverage_on -file "*/rtl/ibex_pkg.sv"

coverage_on -file "*/rtl/ibex_alu.sv"
coverage_on -file "*/rtl/ibex_branch_predict.sv"
coverage_on -file "*/rtl/ibex_compressed_decoder.sv"
